### ============ SETUP ============

### Health (public)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### Register Thato (409 if already registered, which is fine)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Thato Khonkhe", "email": "thato@example.com", "password": "Password123" }

### Register Lerato (409 if already registered, which is fine)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "fullName": "Lerato Mokoena", "email": "lerato@example.com", "password": "Password123" }

### Login as Thato
# @name thato
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "thato@example.com", "password": "Password123" }

### Auto-category: Uber Eats (expect EATING_OUT, source RULE)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-06", "description": "UBER EATS ORDER", "amount": -145.00 }

### Auto-category: unknown expense (expect OTHER, source RULE)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-07", "description": "Something unusual", "amount": -50.00 }

### User's choice wins: Uber but chosen as SHOPPING (expect SHOPPING, source USER)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-08", "description": "Uber gift card", "amount": -200.00, "category": "SHOPPING" }

### Login as Lerato
# @name lerato
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "lerato@example.com", "password": "Password123" }

### ============ THATO'S DATA ============

### Thato creates Rent
# @name rent
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-02", "description": "Rent", "amount": -7500.00, "category": "HOUSING" }

### Thato creates Salary
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-01", "description": "Salary", "amount": 25000.00, "category": "INCOME" }

### Thato lists his transactions (expect 2)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ============ LERATO'S DATA ============

### Lerato creates Groceries
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{lerato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-05", "description": "Pick n Pay groceries", "amount": -900.00, "category": "GROCERIES" }

### Lerato lists her transactions (expect ONLY her 1)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{lerato.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### ============ SECURITY CHECKS ============

### Lerato tries to READ Thato's Rent (expect 404)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{rent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{lerato.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Lerato tries to DELETE Thato's Rent (expect 404)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{rent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{lerato.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Thato can still read his Rent (expect 200)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions/{{rent.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### No token at all (expect 401)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/transactions

### ============ VALIDATION CHECKS ============

### Zero amount (expect 400)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-05", "description": "Mistake", "amount": 0 }

### Missing description (expect 400 with field errors)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{thato.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "date": "2026-09-05", "description": "", "amount": -50.00 }